# NDT / MNDM compact formula summary


PURPOSE:
- machine-oriented compression of the formula layer in
  `articles/compendium/Noetic Diffusion Theory Compendium.typ` (NDT v1.0 formalization)
  and `articles/NoeticDiffusionTheory_v2/Noetic Diffusion Theory - Neural State, Dynamical
  Accessibility, and the Geometry of Possible Futures.typ` (NDT v2)
- prefer symbolic reuse over prose
- use as canonical notation map, not as publication text

CORE SYMBOLS:
- X_t in M                      = latent noetic state on manifold M
- x_t = [m_t, d_t, e_t]^T       = 3D chart state
- x_t^(9)                       = 9D stratified chart state
- Y_t                           = measured neural data
- g                             = measurement map
- epsilon_t                     = observation noise
- G_t(x)                        = effective geometry / conductance tensor
- Phi(x,t)                      = effective potential
- phi_meta(t)                   = slow meta-regulatory field
- sigma(t), Sigma(t)            = diffusion/noise amplitude
- W_t                           = Brownian motion
- J(x,t)                        = Meta-Noetic Jacobian (MNJ)
- S = (J + J^T)/2               = symmetric part
- Omega = (J - J^T)/2           = antisymmetric / rotational part
- A_t, b_t, Q_t                 = local linear reachability parameters
- Sigma_t^(h)                   = h-step reachability covariance
- c_t, gamma                    = contextual/control state; control-or-history protocol on [t,t+h]
- K^h, K^(X|gamma), K^(x|gamma) = finite-horizon transition law (latent / chart-conditional)
- M(x,t|c), V(x,t|c), u_nc      = mobility tensor, NDT potential, non-conservative drift residual
- q_AB(x)                       = committor / destination probability
- alpha(J), omega(J)            = spectral / numerical abscissa of J
- Delta_react                   = omega(J) - alpha(J), reactivity gap

AXIS SEMANTICS:
- m = metastability / mobility / rhythmic coordination
- d = deviation from optimal integration-segregation balance
- e = entropy / entropic energy / complexity pressure
- legacy (E,R,D)-style triplets are treated as monotone-aligned precursors to (m,d,e)

CHARTS:
- x_t = [m_t, d_t, e_t]^T in R^3
- x_t^(9) = [m_a, m_e, m_o, d_n, d_l, d_s, e_e, e_s, e_m]^T in R^9
- Y_t = g(X_t) + epsilon_t

==================================================
1. CORE NDT / MNDM LATENT DYNAMICS
==================================================

MINIMAL MODEL:
- dX_t = -grad F_min(X_t) dt + sigma(t) dW_t
- F_min(X) = e(X) - m(X)
- sigma(t) = sigma_min + sigma_0 (1 - r(t))
- r(t) in [0,1] = rhythmic control; high r => lower noise / stronger denoising

EXTENDED GEOMETRIC MODEL:
- dX_t = -G_t(X_t) grad Phi(X_t,t) dt + sigma(t) dW_t
- Phi(X,t) = alpha(t)e(X) - beta(t)m(X) + gamma(t)d(X) - delta(t)phi_meta(t)
- drift: b(x,t) = -G_t(x) grad Phi(x,t)

GENERAL CONTROLLED-DIFFUSION FORM (NDT v1.0 Compendium / v2 canonical):
- dX_t = b(X_t,t|c_t) dt + Sigma(X_t,t|c_t) dW_t
- c_t = contextual / control state (rhythm, thalamic access, history, body, metabolism)
- effective continuous-state approximation; not a claim of literal Brownian or Markov neural
  dynamics; hybrid / colored-noise / delayed / non-Markov formulations remain compatible

DRIFT SPLIT (MOBILITY TENSOR + NON-CONSERVATIVE RESIDUAL):
- b(xi,t|c) = -M(xi,t|c) grad V(xi,t|c) + u_nc(xi,t|c)
- M >> 0 = mobility tensor (converts a Euclidean gradient into potential-driven drift)
- V = NDT potential (general form; instantiated as Phi(X,t) in the extended geometric model
  above, with M = G_t(x))
- M = g^(-1) if a Riemannian metric g is separately declared
- no assumed fluctuation-dissipation relation linking M to a
- decomposition not uniquely identified from trajectories: state-dependent M can itself
  produce non-symmetric chart Jacobians -> Jacobian asymmetry is NOT sufficient evidence
  of a non-conservative mechanism (u_nc != 0)

GENERATOR:
- L psi(x) = b(x,t) . grad psi(x) + (1/2) Tr(a(x,t) nabla^2 psi(x))
- a(x,t) = Sigma(t) Sigma(t)^T
- control-conditioned form: L_(t|c) f(xi) = b(xi,t|c) . grad f(xi)
  + (1/2) Tr(a(xi,t|c) nabla^2 f(xi)),  a(xi,t|c) = Sigma(xi,t|c) Sigma(xi,t|c)^T

TRANSITION-LAW / KERNEL FAMILY:
- latent protocol-conditional kernel:
  - K_(t:t+h)^(X|gamma)(xi,A) = P(X_(t+h) in A | X_t = xi, gamma_([t:t+h]))
- chart-conditional kernel (what is usually estimated):
  - K_(t:t+h)^(x|gamma)(x,B) = P(x_(t+h) in B | x_t = x, gamma_([t:t+h]))
- gamma = control/history protocol on [t,t+h] (instantaneous c_t, a path of c, or an
  augmented state Z_t = (X_t,C_t,H_t,...) made approximately Markov)
- unadorned K^h means the chart-conditional K^x unless a latent argument is explicit
- K^h = law of the state AT horizon h, not the full path-space measure
- {K^h}_(h>0) is the primary finite-horizon object; a frozen-c_t snapshot kernel is
  only a special case

THREE CORE COMMITMENTS (NDT-C1 / NDT-C2 / NDT-C3):
- NDT-C1 (reduced-state insufficiency): x_t need not determine the latent future law K^X
- NDT-C2 (non-redundant accessibility): functionals of K^x can carry reproducible
  out-of-sample information beyond current x_t and standard static/spectral summaries
- NDT-C3 (conditional control): context/history/physiology can alter K_h^(x|gamma)(. | x)
  among observations matched on current chart state x
- empirical content is C2 + C3, not C1 alone; C1 is a generic sufficiency caveat true of
  almost any coarse chart
- C3 statement: K_h^(x|gamma_1)(x,.) != K_h^(x|gamma_2)(x,.) at matched x
  (stronger than "adding a covariate improves prediction")

NON-EQUIVALENT LOCAL-DYNAMICS FAMILIES (do not conflate):
- b            = infinitesimal conditional mean rate
- a            = infinitesimal conditional covariance rate
- J            = local drift derivative in a declared chart
- reachability = finite-horizon predictive spread (2nd-moment approx of K^h)
- q            = committor / destination (hitting) probability
- attractors   = long-time organization (basins, depth, corridors)
- FAR          = response to a finite (non-infinitesimal) displacement
- rhythm / thalamus / history / body / metabolism are candidate changes to L or K,
  not additional definitions of NDT

EMPIRICAL COARSE DRIFT/DIFFUSION:
- b_hat(x) approx (1/Delta t) E[X_(k+1) - X_k | X_k approx x]
- a_hat(x) approx (1/Delta t) Cov[X_(k+1) - X_k | X_k approx x]

WELL-POSEDNESS ENVELOPE:
- (M,g) complete Riemannian manifold
- Phi(.,t) at least C^2 in state, C^1 in time
- G_t(x) symmetric positive definite, Lipschitz in x
- sigma(t) piecewise continuous, bounded away from 0

IDENTIFIABILITY WARNING:
- data constrain local law / generator more directly than a unique decomposition into (G_t, Phi, sigma)
- gauge freedoms: chart change, time reparametrization, additive constants in Phi

