==================================================
4. META-NOETIC JACOBIAN (MNJ)
==================================================

FLOW:
- f(x,t) = xdot(t)

MNJ DEFINITION:
- J_ij(x,t) = partial f_i(x,t) / partial x_j = partial xdot_i / partial x_j

3D MATRIX:
- J(x,t) =
  [ dmdot/dm  dmdot/dd  dmdot/de
    dddot/dm  dddot/dd  dddot/de
    dedot/dm  dedot/dd  dedot/de ]

CANONICAL DECOMPOSITION:
- S = (1/2)(J + J^T)
- Omega = (1/2)(J - J^T)

DERIVED INVARIANTS:
- Tr(J) = div f
- J v_k = lambda_k v_k
- Jdot = dJ/dt

MODAL GROWTH / REACTIVITY FAMILY (distinct from S/Omega above):
- spectral abscissa: alpha(J) = max_i Re[lambda_i(J)]        (dominant modal growth/decay rate)
- numerical abscissa: omega(J) = lambda_max((J + J^T)/2)     (max instantaneous growth rate)
- reactivity gap: Delta_react(J) = omega(J) - alpha(J)
- alpha < 0 with omega > 0 is possible: all eigenmodes decay while some perturbations
  still grow transiently (established non-normal-network phenomenon; distinct from
  eigenvalue-driven slowing)
- Delta_react is a derived, non-normality-sensitive summary, not a complete non-normality
  measure; Omega supplies a separate rotational component

FINITE-TIME AMPLIFICATION (a further, separate object):
- G_peak(T) = peak gain of the local propagator over a declared horizon T
- does not follow from alpha, omega, or Delta_react alone (instantaneous vs finite-time)
- truth-known simulator recovery of alpha/omega/Delta_react on restricted linear systems is
  a methodological qualification, not empirical chart or biological validation

COORDINATE BOUNDARY:
- J, alpha, omega, Omega are chart-level local summaries in a declared measurement chart
- away from fixed points they are not generally invariant under nonlinear reparametrization;
  a nonlinear chart change induces an Ito correction for an Ito SDE
- current MNJ-derived quantities are chart-level dynamical measurements, not intrinsic
  manifold tensors; an intrinsic (covariant) formulation would need a declared connection
  and is not currently estimated

EMPIRICAL LOCAL LINEAR ESTIMATION:
- xdot approx A(x - xbar) + b
- J_hat = A
- discrete/continuous relation:
  - J_d = exp(J_c Delta t)
  - J_c approx (J_d - I) / Delta t     for small Delta t

RELATION TO POTENTIAL CURVATURE:
- if f(x,t) = -G_t(x) grad Phi(x,t), then
- J(x,t) = -G_t(x) nabla^2 Phi(x,t) - R(x,t)
- R_(i,j)(x,t) = sum_k [partial_j G_(i,k)(x,t)] [partial_k Phi(x,t)]
- common approximation:
  - J(x,t) approx -G_t(x) nabla^2 Phi(x,t)
  - valid only when ||R|| is small relative to ||G_t nabla^2 Phi||

9D / FAMILY-BLOCK JACOBIAN:
- J^(9) =
  [ J_(m,m)  J_(m,d)  J_(m,e)
    J_(d,m)  J_(d,d)  J_(d,e)
    J_(e,m)  J_(e,d)  J_(e,e) ]
- each J_(out,in) in R^(3x3)

